{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/rep_dish_towels","webpackCompilationHash":"8cc9788010e3663b7336","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<!-- TODO:DESCRIPTION — Joe to write. Do not commit while this marker is present. -->\n<p><img src=\"/IMG_0376-0b1c6292ec3fb61b9d3cc3160784963f.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0376.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0406-ee4533b9d37b02328562d900ccf0395b.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0406.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0554-be1f6dfc980af37bcae92b7f12fbc785.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0554.jpg\"></p>","frontmatter":{"path":"/rep_dish_towels","title":"Rep Dish Towels","date":"2026-04-04","tags":["weaving"]}}},"pageContext":{"isCreatedByStatefulCreatePages":false,"prev":{"html":"<!-- TODO:DESCRIPTION — Joe to write. Do not commit while this marker is present. -->\n<p><img src=\"/IMG_0780-972e0ecf340b42dc995c11ca88ed6ad3.png\" alt=\"IMG_0780.png\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0782-3c033419512a2b9087910ea82e457328.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0782.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0792-ddbe32d1823530b8c2756a715ee41d63.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0792.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0795-2bdc308cfce128392c10ed9f8d24b087.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0795.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0805-bbbfe1837a59e454bb45cec7bbaf693a.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0805.jpg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_0820-6762cde8d6e6f20354493f24f55fe26c.jpg\" alt=\"IMG_0820.jpg\"></p>","id":"a927a94f-41d5-5644-af4e-c8499937b9b8","frontmatter":{"path":"/cedar_bracelet","title":"Cedar Bracelet","date":"2026-07-18","tags":["beadwork"],"hexagonImages":["IMG_0780_hexagon.png","IMG_0820_hexagon.jpg"]}},"next":{"html":"<p>Peter Collingwood described this kind of shaft switching device, where levers can be used to move the eye in a \"transit heddle\" between the eyes of two heddles mounted on regular shafts. Carol Irving guided me to the <a href=\"https://handwovenmagazine.com/design-grids-for-samba/\">four-end unit threading</a> described in the article Samba from Handwoven Magazine Nov/Dec 2020.</p>\n<p>Some inferred measurements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lever length 4.375, thickness .4 width 1/2”</li>\n<li>Pivot .475” from end</li>\n<li>Texsolv holes .67” from other end maps</li>\n<li>Side plank .9” x .377  / 3” inside to inside / 4.85” outside to outside / 3.9” on center</li>\n<li>3/16 side rods</li>\n<li>1/4 pivot rod</li>\n<li>L-channel</li>\n<li>.43 in vertical center to center of woods</li>\n<li>Shaft rod: 1.25 x 3/8</li>\n<li>Device width: 47”</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img src=\"/IMG_9167-78f5f3c019e56c51a877180e8ea4e6ce.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9167.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_9168-e0e216e5181598a5db810ec9f2a7f9ab.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9168.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_9169-2df074a7df1b9918a8d71a367cf0f2ca.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9169.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_9315-e03e66a416ae342dbee88837034b3502.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9315.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_9336-1194050481600973a62c325723ae981c.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9336.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_9340-f36f34c8bf47bb785a6cdc9dc7191d33.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_9340.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_4137-644332ddc7f613d9eda72027e0028db3.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_4137.jpeg\">\n<img src=\"/IMG_4139-7ef01a9c73a181ab9da6118417241b2e.jpeg\" alt=\"IMG_4139.jpeg\"></p>","id":"c01db6c7-9333-5347-82c0-b5c64c958c7a","frontmatter":{"path":"/shaft_switching_device","title":"Shaft Switching Device","date":"2025-01-01","tags":["weaving"],"hexagonImages":["IMG_9169_hexagon.jpg","IMG_9168_hexagon.jpg","IMG_9336_hexagon.jpg","IMG_4137_hexagon.jpg","IMG_4139_hexagon.jpg"]}}}}}